IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `eoa-dates`
IMPORT `eoa-work`
IMPORT `eoa-complaints`

-- Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) -- worked cases for the questions of the employee or job applicant and of the
-- complainant.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Helpers: facts by name`

-- The facts of the treatment, by short names: "direct", "associate", "segregated", "former sex", "reasonable", "dog",
-- "requirement", "proportion", "unreasonable", "cannot comply", "reassigned".
GIVEN fs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `The treatment`
`treatment with` fs MEANS `The treatment` WITH
    `treated less favourably because of my attribute` IS elem "direct" fs
    `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` IS elem "associate" fs
    `segregated because of race` IS elem "segregated" fs
    `treated as being of my former sex` IS elem "former sex" fs
    `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` IS elem "reasonable" fs
    `a guide dog or hearing dog` IS elem "dog" fs
    `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` IS elem "requirement" fs
    `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` IS elem "proportion" fs
    `the requirement is not reasonable` IS elem "unreasonable" fs
    `I do not or cannot comply` IS elem "cannot comply" fs
    `I am a gender reassigned person` IS elem "reassigned" fs

-- The exception facts, by short names, with the employer's number of employees.
GIVEN fs IS A LIST OF STRING
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The exception facts`
`exceptions with` fs `and employees` n MEANS `The exception facts` WITH
    `domestic duties where the employer lives` IS elem "domestic" fs
    `the employer's number of employees` IS n
    `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification` IS elem "goq" fs
    `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties` IS elem "enough" fs
    `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding` IS elem "women's rights" fs
    `the job is one of two for a couple` IS elem "couple" fs
    `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs` IS elem "measure" fs
    `the duties involve caring for children where they live` IS elem "children" fs
    `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too` IS elem "spouse" fs
    `a likelihood of collusion with my relative` IS elem "collusion" fs
    `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services` IS elem "authenticity" fs
    `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties` IS elem "religious employer" fs
    `a political job` IS elem "political job" fs
    `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work` IS elem "unable" fs
    `the terms are reasonable given my impairment` IS elem "reasonable terms" fs
    `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations` IS elem "health and safety" fs
    `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme` IS elem "retirement scheme" fs
    `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law` IS elem "youth wages" fs
    `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court` IS elem "court order" fs
    `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice` IS elem "religious body" fs
    `staff of a religious school, in good faith` IS elem "religious school" fs

GIVEN fs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `The religious practice`
`practice with` fs MEANS `The religious practice` WITH
    `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion` IS elem "recognised" fs
    `reasonable to do in working hours` IS elem "reasonable" fs
    `no detriment to the employer` IS elem "no detriment" fs

`all three` MEANS LIST "recognised", "reasonable", "no detriment"

-- The exported discrimination question, asked with a treatment record.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, t IS A `The treatment`
GIVETH AN `Is it discrimination`
`ask meaning` g t MEANS `ss 8 to 67A -- was I discriminated against` g (t's `treated less favourably because of my attribute`) (t's `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute`) (t's `segregated because of race`) (t's `treated as being of my former sex`) (t's `the less favourable treatment was reasonable`) (t's `a guide dog or hearing dog`) (t's `a requirement or condition was imposed on me`) (t's `a substantially higher proportion of others comply`) (t's `the requirement is not reasonable`) (t's `I do not or cannot comply`) (t's `I am a gender reassigned person`)

-- The exported work question, asked with records.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, w IS A `What was done`, t IS A `The treatment`, e IS A `The exception facts`, r IS A `The religious practice`
GIVETH A `Was it unlawful in work`
`ask work` g w t e r MEANS `ss 11 to 67B -- was what my employer did unlawful` g w (t's `treated less favourably because of my attribute`) (t's `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute`) (t's `segregated because of race`) (t's `treated as being of my former sex`) (t's `the less favourable treatment was reasonable`) (t's `a guide dog or hearing dog`) (t's `a requirement or condition was imposed on me`) (t's `a substantially higher proportion of others comply`) (t's `the requirement is not reasonable`) (t's `I do not or cannot comply`) (t's `I am a gender reassigned person`) (e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`) (e's `the employer's number of employees`) (e's `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification`) (e's `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties`) (e's `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding`) (e's `the job is one of two for a couple`) (e's `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`) (e's `the duties involve caring for children where they live`) (e's `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too`) (e's `a likelihood of collusion with my relative`) (e's `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services`) (e's `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties`) (e's `a political job`) (e's `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work`) (e's `the terms are reasonable given my impairment`) (e's `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations`) (e's `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme`) (e's `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law`) (e's `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court`) (e's `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice`) (e's `staff of a religious school, in good faith`) (r's `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion`) (r's `reasonable to do in working hours`) (r's `no detriment to the employer`)

`none` MEANS EMPTY
`no exceptions` MEANS `exceptions with` EMPTY `and employees` 20
`no practice` MEANS `practice with` EMPTY
`direct` MEANS `treatment with` (LIST "direct")

§ `Short names for the dates used below`

`15 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar day` 15 3 2025
`15 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 15 3 2026
`16 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 16 3 2026
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 29 2 2024
`28 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar day` 28 2 2025
`1 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 3 2025
`31 Aug 2025` MEANS `the calendar day` 31 8 2025
`28 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 28 2 2026
`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 3 2026
`10 Jan 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 10 1 2026
`10 Jul 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 10 7 2026
`11 Jul 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 11 7 2026
`3 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 3 2 2026
`24 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 24 2 2026
`25 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 25 2 2026
`31 Jan 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 31 1 2026
`21 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 21 2 2026
`1 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 10 2026
`22 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 22 10 2026
`23 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 23 10 2026
`10 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar day` 10 3 2025

§ `The dates module`

-- 15 March 2025 plus 12 months: 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT `15 Mar 2025` `plus calendar months` 12 EQUALS `15 Mar 2026`
-- 29 February 2024 plus 12 months: February 2025 has no 29th, so 28 February 2025 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `29 Feb 2024` `plus calendar months` 12 EQUALS `28 Feb 2025`
-- 31 August 2025 plus 6 months: 28 February 2026 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `31 Aug 2025` `plus calendar months` 6 EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
-- 31 January 2026 plus 21 days: 21 February 2026.
#ASSERT `31 Jan 2026` `plus days` 21 EQUALS `21 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `the number of days from` `3 Feb 2026` `until` `24 Feb 2026` EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `the day number of` `1 Mar 2025` `counted from` `15 Mar 2025` EQUALS 0

§ `s 4(1) -- the Act's own terms`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a gender reassigned person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I hold a recognition certificate or an equivalent certificate (s 4(1), paragraph (a))`
-- The 2024 amendment (No. 31 of 2024): a birth registration changed under s 36Q is enough.
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a gender reassigned person` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the sex or gender in my birth registration has been changed under s 36Q of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (s 4(1), paragraph (b)(i))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a gender reassigned person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I have been issued a document acknowledging my sex or gender under s 36ZA of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (s 4(1), paragraph (b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a gender reassigned person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a gender reassigned person means only a person with one of those certificates, changes or documents (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have an impairment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I have, or had in the past, an impairment as s 4(1) defines it`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have an impairment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I have, or had in the past, an impairment as s 4(1) defines it`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have an impairment` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: an impairment is imputed to me (s 4(1), paragraph (e))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have an impairment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: none of the conditions in s 4(1) (a) to (c) is present, past or imputed (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have a family responsibility or family status` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I have responsibility for the care of another person, other than in paid employment (s 4(1), paragraph (a))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have a family responsibility or family status` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I have the status of being a particular relative, or a relative of a particular person (s 4(1), paragraphs (b) and (c))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- do I have a family responsibility or family status` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: caring only in the course of paid employment, and no relative status, is outside the definition (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

§ `ss 5, 8 to 67A -- the meaning of discrimination`

#ASSERT `ask meaning` `sex` `direct` EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment on the ground" "s 8(1)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `breast feeding or bottle feeding` `direct` EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment on the ground" "s 10A(1)"
-- Pregnancy: less favourable treatment found reasonable is not direct discrimination (s 10(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `pregnancy` (`treatment with` (LIST "direct", "reasonable")) EQUALS `not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the definition's "if" is not met: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `pregnancy` `direct` EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment on the ground" "s 10(1)"
-- "reasonable" matters for pregnancy only: for sex it is ignored.
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `sex` (`treatment with` (LIST "direct", "reasonable")) EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment on the ground" "s 8(1)"
-- Indirect: all three limbs.
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `sex` (`treatment with` (LIST "requirement", "proportion", "unreasonable", "cannot comply")) EQUALS `discrimination` "indirect: a requirement or condition" "s 8(2)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `age` (`treatment with` (LIST "requirement", "proportion", "unreasonable", "cannot comply")) EQUALS `discrimination` "indirect: a requirement or condition" "s 66V(3)"
-- One limb missing (the requirement is reasonable): not indirect discrimination.
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `sex` (`treatment with` (LIST "requirement", "proportion", "cannot comply")) EQUALS `not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the definition's "if" is not met: the text's no)`
-- s 67A(b): an unreasonable requirement is enough, without the proportion or compliance limbs.
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` (`treatment with` (LIST "requirement", "unreasonable")) EQUALS `discrimination` "indirect: a requirement or condition that is not reasonable" "s 67A(b)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` `direct` EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment on the ground" "s 67A(a)"
-- Relative or associate: for sexual orientation, race and impairment only.
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `sexual orientation` (`treatment with` (LIST "associate")) EQUALS `discrimination` `the associate kind` "s 35O(2)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `impairment` (`treatment with` (LIST "associate")) EQUALS `discrimination` `the associate kind` "s 66A(1a)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `age` (`treatment with` (LIST "associate")) EQUALS `not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the definition's "if" is not met: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `race` (`treatment with` (LIST "segregated")) EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: segregation on the ground of race" "s 36(1)(e) or (1a)(e)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `impairment` (`treatment with` (LIST "dog")) EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment because of a guide dog or hearing dog" "s 66A(4)"
-- Gender history: only a gender reassigned person.
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `gender history` `direct` EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: Part IIAA reaches only a gender reassigned person; the Act does not say what else applies`
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `gender history` (`treatment with` (LIST "direct", "reassigned")) EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment on the ground" "s 35AB(1)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `gender history` (`treatment with` (LIST "former sex", "reassigned")) EQUALS `discrimination` "direct: treated as being of the former sex" "s 35AB(3)(a)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `gender history` (`treatment with` (LIST "requirement", "proportion", "unreasonable", "cannot comply", "reassigned")) EQUALS `discrimination` "indirect: a requirement or condition" "s 35AB(3)(b)"
#ASSERT `ask meaning` `religious conviction` (`treatment with` none) EQUALS `not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the definition's "if" is not met: the text's no)`

§ `ss 11 to 67B -- was what my employer did unlawful`

-- Dismissed because of sex: unlawful under s 11(2)(c).
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `by dismissing me` `direct` `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(2)(c)" "s 8(1)"
-- Pregnancy: dismissal found reasonable is not discrimination; found not reasonable, unlawful.
#ASSERT `ask work` `pregnancy` `by dismissing me` (`treatment with` (LIST "direct", "reasonable")) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ask work` `pregnancy` `by dismissing me` `direct` `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(2)(c)" "s 10(1)"
-- Indirect sex discrimination in the terms of employment (a full-time requirement fewer women can meet).
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` (`treatment with` (LIST "requirement", "proportion", "unreasonable", "cannot comply")) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(2)(a)" "s 8(2)"
-- A job refused because of a fines website listing, by an unreasonable requirement: s 67B(1)(b).
#ASSERT `ask work` `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` `in deciding who should be offered employment` (`treatment with` (LIST "requirement", "unreasonable")) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 67B(1)(b)" "s 67A(b)"
-- Dismissed because of a partner's race only: s 37 speaks of the person's own race (fork F3).
#ASSERT `ask work` `race` `by dismissing me` (`treatment with` (LIST "associate")) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `NOTHING-kind` "s 37 forbids discrimination on the ground of the person's own attribute; whether discrimination through a relative or associate falls within it is not said (fork F3)"
-- Own race and segregation: unlawful.
#ASSERT `ask work` `race` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` (`treatment with` (LIST "segregated")) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 37(2)(a)" "s 36(1)(e) or (1a)(e)"
-- Gender history: not a gender reassigned person.
#ASSERT `ask work` `gender history` `by dismissing me` `direct` `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `NOTHING-kind` "s 35AC protects only a gender reassigned person (s 4(1)); whether other law reaches this is outside this Act"
#ASSERT `ask work` `gender history` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` (`treatment with` (LIST "former sex", "reassigned")) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 35AC(2)(a)" "s 35AB(3)(a)"
-- Nothing less favourable shown: not discrimination.
#ASSERT `ask work` `age` `by dismissing me` (`treatment with` none) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the text's no)`
-- A guide dog: job refused.
#ASSERT `ask work` `impairment` `in deciding who should be offered employment` (`treatment with` (LIST "dog")) `no exceptions` `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 66B(1)(b)" "s 66A(4)"

§ `s 54(3) -- a religious practice refused`

#ASSERT `ask work` `religious conviction` `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours` (`treatment with` none) `no exceptions` (`practice with` `all three`) EQUALS `unlawful` "s 54(3)" "s 54(3) itself (fork F2)"
-- One condition missing: the practice would subject the employer to a detriment.
#ASSERT `ask work` `religious conviction` `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours` (`treatment with` none) `no exceptions` (`practice with` (LIST "recognised", "reasonable")) EQUALS `not unlawful under s 54(3): the practice is not one the subsection protects (the text's no)`
-- Five employees: s 54(4)(b) ("does not exceed 5"). Six: unlawful.
#ASSERT `ask work` `religious conviction` `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours` (`treatment with` none) (`exceptions with` none `and employees` 5) (`practice with` `all three`) EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 54(4)(b): the employer employs no more than 5 persons, not counting domestic workers"
#ASSERT `ask work` `religious conviction` `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours` (`treatment with` none) (`exceptions with` none `and employees` 6) (`practice with` `all three`) EQUALS `unlawful` "s 54(3)" "s 54(3) itself (fork F2)"
-- The small-employer exception reaches religious and political conviction only: a 3-person employer is bound for sex.
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` none `and employees` 3) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(2)(c)" "s 8(1)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `political conviction` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` none `and employees` 3) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 54(4)(b): the employer employs no more than 5 persons, not counting domestic workers"
#ASSERT `ask work` `political conviction` `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours` (`treatment with` none) `no exceptions` (`practice with` `all three`) EQUALS `NOTHING-kind` "s 54(3) is about refusing a religious practice on the ground of religious conviction; choose another thing done for this ground"

§ `The exceptions`

-- Domestic duties: s 11(3) covers sex in the choice of whom to employ only.
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "domestic") `and employees` 1) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 11(3): domestic duties on the premises where the employer resides (choice of whom to employ only)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "domestic") `and employees` 1) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(2)(c)" "s 8(1)"
-- No domestic exception for marital status (finding 3).
#ASSERT `ask work` `marital status` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "domestic") `and employees` 1) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(1)(b)" "s 9(1)"
-- Gender history: s 35AC(3) covers employees too.
#ASSERT `ask work` `gender history` `by dismissing me` (`treatment with` (LIST "direct", "reassigned")) (`exceptions with` (LIST "domestic") `and employees` 1) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 35AC(3): domestic duties within a private household in which the employer resides"
-- Age: s 66W(3) covers applicants only; terms offered count.
#ASSERT `ask work` `age` `in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "domestic") `and employees` 1) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 66W(3): domestic duties within a private household in which the employer resides (applicants only)"
-- s 27: a genuine occupational qualification, unless s 27(3).
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "goq") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 27: being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification for the position"
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "goq", "enough") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(1)(b)" "s 8(1)"
-- s 27 does not reach the terms on which employment is offered.
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "goq") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(1)(c)" "s 8(1)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `sex` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "women's rights") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 28: rights or privileges granted to women in connection with pregnancy, childbirth, breast feeding or bottle feeding"
#ASSERT `ask work` `marital status` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "couple") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 29: a job which is one of 2 to be held by a married couple or de facto partners"
#ASSERT `ask work` `race` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "measure") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 51: a measure intended to achieve equality"
-- No special-measures exception for publication on the fines website.
#ASSERT `ask work` `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "measure") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 67B(1)(b)" "s 67A(a)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `marital status` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "children", "spouse") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 33(2): residential care of children, where the occupant's spouse is also to be employed"
#ASSERT `ask work` `marital status` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "children") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 11(2)(c)" "s 9(1)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `family responsibility or family status` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "collusion") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 35M: a demonstrated significant likelihood of collusion with a relative, damaging the employer's business"
#ASSERT `ask work` `race` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "authenticity") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 50: genuine occupational qualification (authenticity, or welfare services best given by a person of the same race)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `political conviction` `in deciding who should be offered employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "political job") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 66(2): offering a political job (electoral officer, ministerial adviser, party worker, electoral staff)"
-- s 66(2) reaches only the offering of employment: a political employee dismissed for politics is within s 54(2)(c).
#ASSERT `ask work` `political conviction` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "political job") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 54(2)(c)" "s 53(1)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `impairment` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "unable") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 66Q(1): reasonable to conclude the person could not do the work reasonably required, or would need services or facilities imposing unjustifiable hardship"
-- s 66Q(1) does not reach terms of employment; s 66Q(2) does.
#ASSERT `ask work` `impairment` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "unable") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 66B(2)(a)" "s 66A(1)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `impairment` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "reasonable terms") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 66Q(2): terms or conditions reasonable having regard to the limitation the impairment imposes, or the services or facilities needed"
#ASSERT `ask work` `age` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "health and safety") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 66ZM: terms and conditions imposed to comply with reasonable health and safety considerations"
#ASSERT `ask work` `age` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "health and safety") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `unlawful` "s 66W(2)(c)" "s 66V(1)"
#ASSERT `ask work` `age` `by subjecting me to any other detriment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "retirement scheme") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 66ZN(1): an offer of a voluntary retirement, retirement incentive, severance or like scheme"
#ASSERT `ask work` `age` `in the terms or conditions of my employment` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "youth wages") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 66ZS(1): necessary to comply with a youth wages or ratio provision of an award, agreement or the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993, or a written law in force when Part IVB began"
#ASSERT `ask work` `sexual orientation` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "court order") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 69: necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or of a court"
#ASSERT `ask work` `sexual orientation` `by dismissing me` `direct` (`exceptions with` (LIST "religious school") `and employees` 20) `no practice` EQUALS `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` "s 73(1): staff of a religious educational institution, in good faith to avoid injury to adherents' religious susceptibilities"

§ `ss 24, 49A -- harassment`

-- A customer harasses an employee sexually: s 24(1)(a) reaches "an employee of that or any other person".
#ASSERT `s 24 -- was I sexually harassed unlawfully` `I am an employee and the harasser is not my employer or a fellow employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `unlawful harassment` "s 24(1)(a): an employee of that or any other person"
#ASSERT `s 24 -- was I sexually harassed unlawfully` `I was seeking work with someone other than the harasser or the harasser's employer` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `unlawful harassment` "s 24(1)(b): a person seeking employment by that or any other person"
#ASSERT `s 24 -- was I sexually harassed unlawfully` `the harasser works for my employer too` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not harassment as the Act defines it (the "if" is not met: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- was I sexually harassed unlawfully` `the harasser is my employer` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not harassment as the Act defines it (the "if" is not met: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 49A -- was I racially harassed unlawfully` `the harasser is my employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `unlawful harassment` "s 49A(1)(a): an employee of the harasser"
#ASSERT `s 49A -- was I racially harassed unlawfully` `the harasser works for my employer too` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `unlawful harassment` "s 49A(1)(b): an employee of a person by whom the harasser is employed"
#ASSERT `s 49A -- was I racially harassed unlawfully` `I was seeking work with the harasser or the harasser's employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `unlawful harassment` "s 49A(1)(c): a person seeking employment by the harasser or by an employer of the harasser"
-- A customer harasses an employee racially: outside s 49A(1) (finding 4).
#ASSERT `s 49A -- was I racially harassed unlawfully` `I am an employee and the harasser is not my employer or a fellow employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind` "s 49A(1) names only the harasser's own employees, fellow employees and job seekers; racial harassment by a customer, client or stranger is not within it (finding 4)"
#ASSERT `s 49A -- was I racially harassed unlawfully` `the harasser is my employer` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not harassment as the Act defines it (the "if" is not met: the text's no)`

§ `s 67 -- victimisation`

#ASSERT `s 67 -- was I victimised` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: unlawful victimisation (s 67(1))`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- was I victimised` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: unlawful victimisation (s 67(1))`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- was I victimised` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 67(1)(f) does not apply, as the allegation was proved false and not made in good faith (s 67(2): the text's no)`
-- s 67(2) takes away paragraph (f) only: a detriment for having complained is still victimisation.
#ASSERT `s 67 -- was I victimised` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: unlawful victimisation (s 67(1))`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- was I victimised` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: s 67 forbids a detriment or threat on the listed grounds only; these facts are outside it`

§ `ss 160, 161 -- who is answerable`

#ASSERT `s 161 -- is the employer answerable` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act applies to the employer or principal as if it had also done the act (s 161(1))`
#ASSERT `s 161 -- is the employer answerable` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the employer or principal established that it took all reasonable steps to prevent acts of that kind (s 161(2): the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 161 -- is the employer answerable` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the act was not done in connection with the employment or the agency (s 161(1)'s "where" is not met: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 160 -- is that person answerable too` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: taken also to have done the act (s 160)`
#ASSERT `s 160 -- is that person answerable too` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: s 160 reaches only a person who caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted the act`

§ `s 83 -- who may lodge`

#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `I would, for myself (and perhaps for others too)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes` "s 83(1)(a)"
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `I would, together with one or more others` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes` "s 83(1)(b)"
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `a trade union of which I am a member` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes` "s 83(1)(c)"
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `a person I authorise, as my impairment means I cannot write or sign my name` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes` "s 83(1a)(a)"
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `a person with a proper interest in my care and protection, as my impairment means I cannot authorise anyone` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes` "s 83(1a)(b)"
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `a person with a proper interest in my care and protection, as my impairment means I cannot authorise anyone` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind` "s 83(1a)(b) needs the Commissioner to be satisfied of the person's proper interest; until then it does not reach the case"
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `someone else` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind` "s 83(1) and (1a) list who may lodge; the list is not closed with 'only', but names no one else"
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `I would, for myself (and perhaps for others too)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a contravention for which a specific penalty is imposed is not one s 83 lets you complain of ("other than": the text's no, fork F5)`
#ASSERT `s 83 -- who may lodge my complaint` `I would, for myself (and perhaps for others too)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind` "s 83(1) provides for a complaint lodged in writing; it says nothing of any other"

§ `s 83(4), (5) -- in time`

#ASSERT `s 83(4) -- the last day to lodge` `15 Mar 2025` EQUALS `15 Mar 2026`
-- Lodged on the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `s 83(4) -- is my complaint in time` `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2026` FALSE EQUALS `in time: lodged within 12 months after the alleged contravention (s 83(4))`
-- One day later: late.
#ASSERT `s 83(4) -- is my complaint in time` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Mar 2026` FALSE EQUALS `late: lodged more than 12 months after the alleged contravention, and not accepted under s 83(5) (s 83(4)'s period: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 83(4) -- is my complaint in time` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Mar 2026` TRUE EQUALS `late, but the Commissioner has accepted it on good cause being shown (s 83(5))`
-- Lodged the same day as the contravention: in time.
#ASSERT `s 83(4) -- is my complaint in time` `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` FALSE EQUALS `in time: lodged within 12 months after the alleged contravention (s 83(4))`
-- 29 February 2024: the last day is 28 February 2025 (fork F1); 1 March 2025 is late.
#ASSERT `s 83(4) -- is my complaint in time` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2025` FALSE EQUALS `in time: lodged within 12 months after the alleged contravention (s 83(4))`
#ASSERT `s 83(4) -- is my complaint in time` `29 Feb 2024` `1 Mar 2025` FALSE EQUALS `late: lodged more than 12 months after the alleged contravention, and not accepted under s 83(5) (s 83(4)'s period: the text's no)`

§ `s 83B -- the industrial route`

#ASSERT `s 83B -- does the industrial route stop my complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a complaint cannot be made under s 83 about this allegation (s 83B(2): the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 83B -- does the industrial route stop my complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the industrial referral or application was withdrawn or failed for want of jurisdiction, so s 83B no longer stops the complaint (s 83B(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 83B -- does the industrial route stop my complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 83B does not stop this complaint`
#ASSERT `s 83B -- does the industrial route stop my complaint` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 83B does not stop this complaint`

§ `s 83A -- withdrawal, lapse and pursuing afresh`

#ASSERT `s 83A(1) -- may I withdraw my complaint` FALSE EQUALS `yes: by notice in writing served on the Commissioner (s 83A(1))`
#ASSERT `s 83A(1) -- may I withdraw my complaint` TRUE EQUALS `no: the complaint has been finally disposed of under Division 2 of Part VII (s 83A(1)'s period: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 83A(2) -- the last day to answer the lapse warning` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `22 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `s 83A(3) -- has my complaint lapsed` `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `22 Oct 2026` EQUALS `no: you served notice within the 21 days, so it does not lapse (s 83A(2))`
#ASSERT `s 83A(3) -- has my complaint lapsed` `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `23 Oct 2026` EQUALS `yes` `22 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `s 83A(3) -- has my complaint lapsed` `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `yes` `22 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `s 83A(4) -- the last day to pursue it afresh` `10 Jan 2026` EQUALS `10 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `s 83A(4) -- may I pursue my complaint afresh` `10 Jan 2026` `10 Jul 2026` TRUE EQUALS `yes: within 6 months and with the Commissioner satisfied of good cause; no new complaint is needed (s 83A(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `s 83A(4) -- may I pursue my complaint afresh` `10 Jan 2026` `11 Jul 2026` TRUE EQUALS `no: more than 6 months from the withdrawal or lapse (s 83A(4)(d)'s period: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 83A(4) -- may I pursue my complaint afresh` `10 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Commissioner is not satisfied that there is good cause (s 83A(4)(c), "unless": the text's no)`

§ `ss 89, 90 -- dismissal and referral`

#ASSERT `s 89 -- can my complaint be dismissed` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Commissioner may dismiss it by written notice giving the reason and your rights under s 90 (s 89)`
#ASSERT `s 89 -- can my complaint be dismissed` FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: s 89 gives no power to dismiss on these facts; the Commissioner must investigate (s 84) and try conciliation where it may succeed (s 91)`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) -- the last day to require referral` `3 Feb 2026` EQUALS `24 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `s 90 -- must my dismissed complaint be referred` `3 Feb 2026` `24 Feb 2026` EQUALS `yes: the Commissioner must refer it to the Tribunal with a report on the investigation (s 90(2))`
#ASSERT `s 90 -- must my dismissed complaint be referred` `3 Feb 2026` `25 Feb 2026` EQUALS `no: the notice was served more than 21 days after you received the dismissal notice (s 90(1)'s period: the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 90 -- must my dismissed complaint be referred` `3 Feb 2026` `3 Feb 2026` EQUALS `yes: the Commissioner must refer it to the Tribunal with a report on the investigation (s 90(2))`

§ `ss 91, 92, 93 -- conciliation and referral`

#ASSERT `ss 91, 93 -- will my complaint go to the Tribunal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not by s 93: it was dismissed under s 89; you may require referral within 21 days under s 90`
#ASSERT `ss 91, 93 -- will my complaint go to the Tribunal` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not by s 93: the complaint was resolved by conciliation`
#ASSERT `ss 91, 93 -- will my complaint go to the Tribunal` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes` "s 93(1)(a): the Commissioner must refer it, with a report"
#ASSERT `ss 91, 93 -- will my complaint go to the Tribunal` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes` "s 93(1)(b): the Commissioner must refer it, with a report"
#ASSERT `ss 91, 93 -- will my complaint go to the Tribunal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes` "s 93(1)(c): the Commissioner must refer it, with a report"
#ASSERT `ss 91, 93 -- will my complaint go to the Tribunal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not yet: the Commissioner must try to resolve it by conciliation (s 91(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 91, 93 -- will my complaint go to the Tribunal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: none of the s 93(1) occasions has arisen yet`
#ASSERT `s 92 -- may they appear for me in conciliation` `myself` FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are entitled to appear personally (s 92(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 92 -- may they appear for me in conciliation` `an agent who is not a lawyer` FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are entitled to appear by an agent other than a lawyer, who may not charge a fee or reward (s 92(1)(a), (2))`
#ASSERT `s 92 -- may they appear for me in conciliation` `a lawyer (solicitor or counsel)` TRUE EQUALS `yes: with the Commissioner's leave you may be represented by a lawyer (s 92(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 92 -- may they appear for me in conciliation` `a lawyer (solicitor or counsel)` FALSE EQUALS `no: a lawyer may represent you only by leave of the Commissioner (s 92(1)(b): the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 93(2) -- will the Commissioner help me at the Tribunal` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Commissioner must help you present your case, and may contribute to witness and other expenses (s 93(2)(a), (b))`
#ASSERT `s 93(2) -- will the Commissioner help me at the Tribunal` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Commissioner must help you present your case (s 93(2)(a)); no contribution to expenses has been found appropriate`
-- Referred because the complainant required it after a dismissal (s 90): s 93(2) does not reach it (finding 6).
#ASSERT `s 93(2) -- will the Commissioner help me at the Tribunal` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: s 93(2) applies to a complaint referred under s 93(1) on your request; a complaint referred because you required it under s 90 is not within it (finding 6)`

§ `ss 107, 126, 127, 134 -- the Tribunal`

#ASSERT `s 107 -- will the Tribunal hold an inquiry` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Tribunal must hold an inquiry; no fee is payable, and the respondent must prove any exception it relies on (ss 107(3), (5), 123)`
#ASSERT `s 107 -- will the Tribunal hold an inquiry` TRUE EQUALS `no: you have told the Tribunal you do not wish the inquiry to be held or to continue, so it must not hold it, or must stop (s 107(3a): the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 126 -- may I apply for an interim order` TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may apply to the Tribunal for an interim order to preserve the status quo or the parties' rights until the complaint is determined (s 126)`
#ASSERT `s 126 -- may I apply for an interim order` FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: s 126 lets a party apply at any time after the complaint is lodged; before then it does not reach the case`
#ASSERT `s 127 -- what can the Tribunal order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST "dismiss the complaint (s 127(a))"
#ASSERT `s 127 -- what can the Tribunal order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS LIST "damages of up to $40,000 for loss or damage suffered by reason of the respondent's conduct (s 127(b)(i))", "an order enjoining the respondent from continuing or repeating the unlawful conduct (s 127(b)(ii))", "an order that the respondent perform a reasonable act or course of conduct to redress your loss or damage (s 127(b)(iii))", "an order declaring void a contract or agreement made in contravention of the Act (s 127(b)(iv))", "decline to take any further action (s 127(b)(v))"
#ASSERT `s 127 -- what can the Tribunal order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST "an order enjoining the respondent from continuing or repeating the unlawful conduct (s 127(b)(ii))", "an order declaring void a contract or agreement made in contravention of the Act (s 127(b)(iv))", "decline to take any further action (s 127(b)(v))"
#ASSERT `s 127(b)(i) -- the most damages I can be awarded` 25000 FALSE EQUALS 25000
#ASSERT `s 127(b)(i) -- the most damages I can be awarded` 40000 FALSE EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `s 127(b)(i) -- the most damages I can be awarded` 40001 FALSE EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `s 127(b)(i) -- the most damages I can be awarded` 150000 FALSE EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `s 127(b)(i) -- the most damages I can be awarded` 25000 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 134 -- may I appeal` TRUE EQUALS `yes: under s 105 of the State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (s 134(1)); that Act sets the leave and the time`
#ASSERT `s 134 -- may I appeal` FALSE EQUALS `NOTHING-kind: s 134(1) speaks only of a party aggrieved by a decision or order under s 126 or s 127`

§ `s 165 -- telling people about a sexual harassment complaint`

#ASSERT `s 165 -- may I tell them about my complaint` TRUE FALSE `anyone else (for example a friend, a colleague, the media or social media)` EQUALS `no: until the Commissioner has begun to investigate, you must not record or pass on any particulars of the complaint to this person; penalty up to $1,000 (s 165(1): the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 165 -- may I tell them about my complaint` TRUE FALSE `a near relative` EQUALS `yes` "s 165(2)(c)(iii)"
#ASSERT `s 165 -- may I tell them about my complaint` TRUE FALSE `the person I complained about` EQUALS `yes` "s 165(2)(b)(ii)"
#ASSERT `s 165 -- may I tell them about my complaint` TRUE FALSE `a person giving me professional treatment, counselling or advice` EQUALS `yes` "s 165(2)(c)(iv)"
#ASSERT `s 165 -- may I tell them about my complaint` TRUE TRUE `anyone else (for example a friend, a colleague, the media or social media)` EQUALS `s 165 does not restrict this` "the bar in s 165(1) lasts only until the Commissioner has commenced to investigate"
#ASSERT `s 165 -- may I tell them about my complaint` FALSE FALSE `anyone else (for example a friend, a colleague, the media or social media)` EQUALS `s 165 does not restrict this` "s 165 applies only to a complaint of sexual harassment under Division 4 of Part II"
